## Validation Timing Patterns

### ✅ Validate on Blur (Recommended for Most Fields)
**When**: After user leaves the field (blur event)
**Best for**: Text inputs, email, phone numbers
**Why**: Doesn't interrupt typing, validates complete input

```typescript
<input onBlur={validateField} />
```

### ✅ Validate on Input (Real-Time)
**When**: As user types (keystroke by keystroke)
**Best for**: Passwords, usernames, character limits
**Why**: Immediate feedback for length/format requirements

```typescript
<input onChange={validateField} />
```

### ✅ Validate on Submit
**When**: When user submits the form
**Best for**: Final check, server-side validation
**Why**: Catches edge cases, enforces completeness

```typescript
<form onSubmit={validateAllFields} />
```

### ❌ Avoid: Validation on Focus
**Why**: Premature - user hasn't entered anything yet
**Exception**: Pre-fill detection (show format example)

## Grammarly-Style Validation Levels

| Severity | Color | When to Use | Example |
|----------|-------|-------------|---------|
| **Error** | 🔴 Red | Blocks submission, critical issues | Invalid email format, missing required field |
| **Warning** | 🟡 Yellow | Doesn't block, but worth reviewing | Weak password, potential typo (email ending in .co) |
| **Suggestion** | 🔵 Blue | Optional improvements | Password could be longer, consider adding 2FA |

## Pattern Comparison

| Pattern | Error Detection | User Experience | Learning |
|---------|----------------|-----------------|----------|
| **No Validation** | ❌ Errors persist | ⚠️ Frustration on submit | ❌ No feedback |
| **Validate on Submit** | ⚠️ Late detection | ⚠️ Context switching | ⚠️ Vague errors |
| **Validate on Blur** | ✅ Early detection | ✅ No interruption | ✅ Immediate feedback |
| **Real-Time (Grammarly)** | ✅ Instant detection | ✅ Flow maintained | ✅ Contextual learning |

For Grammarly specifically, the cited documentation supports automatic checking, inline
underlines, categorized suggestions, review cards, explanations, and accept/dismiss controls.
Whether those behaviors reduce errors or proofreading time must be measured for a defined
writing task; the historical audience figure is not an effectiveness metric.

